            "review_text": "CC01234\nBangkok, Thailand1 contribution\n0\nPerfection\nApr 2019 • Couples\nWe have been travelling Vietnam for a couple weeks now and were really craving some Western food. Luckily we met other travellers who were staying at Azerai and they told us about the resort which is on private little island in the river in front of Can Tho city. We made a reservation and they took us across by boat (for free), a quick 3 minutes ride. The island seems really beautiful, very elegant, green and calm with these absolutely stunning banyan trees. We were a bit early so we started with sunset cocktails by the pond (highly recommend this). For dinner I had tenderloin steak with pepper sauce and mashed potato, my husband had grilled chicken breast with lemon butter and asparagus. Both were perfectly cooked. And they had good, reasonably priced wine by the glass, which has been a big challenge to find so far on this trip. But what makes this place so recommendable is the lovely relaxed ambience and friendly service. They really made us feel welcome and special. We have 1 more night in Can Tho and will be coming back to try their Vietnamese restaurant -- we made the reservation for it on the spot!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 21, 2019",
